wing{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pirut","id":19351845,"login":"pirut","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MzUxODQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/1541d7246513d052c647088b18cfcd945da847a2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T20:18:28Z","email":"scottbussardjr@gmail.com","name":"JR Bussard"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T20:18:28Z","email":"scottbussardjr@gmail.com","name":"JR Bussard"},"message":"Actually use the Suspense wrapper the lazy route needs\n\nThe previous commit added an AdventureBay component to wrap the lazily\nloaded game in a Suspense boundary, then left the route entry pointing at\nthe bare lazy component. Two consequences: React.lazy without a boundary is\na runtime error waiting on that route, and the unused wrapper tripped\nno-unused-vars — which Create React App promotes to a build failure whenever\nCI is set, as it is on Vercel. The deploy never produced a bundle.\n\nVerified this time against `CI=true npm run build` and the served build\nrather than a dev server, since that is what actually ships.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"00c9b178d7459805306e5a2abf10ea76f6049de2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/git/trees/00c9b178d7459805306e5a2abf10ea76f6049de2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/git/commits/1541d7246513d052c647088b18cfcd945da847a2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19351845?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pirut","id":19351845,"login":"pirut","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MzUxODQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/pirut/jrbussard/commit/1541d7246513d052c647088b18cfcd945da847a2","node_id":"C_kwDOMtjVTdoAKDE1NDFkNzI0NjUxM2QwNTJjNjQ3MDg4YjE4Y2ZjZDk0NWRhODQ3YTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/pirut/jrbussard/commit/3eb0812a597926a07cdf379e5813a25df50bd878","sha":"3eb0812a597926a07cdf379e5813a25df50bd878","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/3eb0812a597926a07cdf379e5813a25df50bd878"}],"sha":"1541d7246513d052c647088b18cfcd945da847a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/1541d7246513d052c647088b18cfcd945da847a2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19351845?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pirut","id":19351845,"login":"pirut","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MzUxODQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/3eb0812a597926a07cdf379e5813a25df50bd878/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T20:07:12Z","email":"scottbussardjr@gmail.com","name":"JR Bussard"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T20:07:12Z","email":"scottbussardjr@gmail.com","name":"JR Bussard"},"message":"Put the rescue pups in a 3D island you can drive around\n\nAdventure Bay: an open world on Three.js where you play any of seven pups,\ndrive their trucks, and take rescues that are generated fresh every time.\nNo downloaded assets — every mesh, texture and sound is made in the browser\nat load.\n\nThe island is one height function. Roads are splines laid over it: a\nrasterisation pass stamps each into a grid of \"how much road is here\" and\n\"what height does the road want\", and the ground is the raw terrain blended\ntoward that. The uphill side gets cut and the downhill side filled for free,\nso the mountain road is a notch someone carved rather than a stripe painted\non a slope. Grades are capped and junctions reconciled, so roads that meet\nagree where they meet.\n\nVehicles are proper rigid bodies with four raycast wheels on springs. They\nsquat under power, lean into corners, unload the inside wheels and land\nnose-first off a jump, none of it scripted. Two things had to be tuned away\nfrom strict physics: cornering forces are applied at a roll centre rather\nthan at the contact patch, and roll rate is damped — at the true lever arm a\ntop-heavy truck lies down in every corner, which is not what this is for.\n\nMissions are generated rather than authored. Nine templates choose their own\nlocations from the road network, decide how many of a thing there are, how\nlong you get, which pup is needed and what it is all called. Underneath they\nshare one shape — an ordered list of objectives, each a place to be and a\nthing to do there — which is what lets them share one loop and one HUD.\n\nThe route is loaded on demand. Three.js is bigger than the rest of the site\nput together and almost nobody arriving at the front page is going to open\nit, so the main bundle is unchanged at 179 kB and the game arrives in its\nown chunk.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c6967835c340258cf9b6e6688c2d3ad9d4b2600b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/git/trees/c6967835c340258cf9b6e6688c2d3ad9d4b2600b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/git/commits/3eb0812a597926a07cdf379e5813a25df50bd878","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19351845?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pirut","id":19351845,"login":"pirut","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MzUxODQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/pirut/jrbussard/commit/3eb0812a597926a07cdf379e5813a25df50bd878","node_id":"C_kwDOMtjVTdoAKDNlYjA4MTJhNTk3OTI2YTA3Y2RmMzc5ZTU4MTNhMjVkZjUwYmQ4Nzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/pirut/jrbussard/commit/4ca3691af6d41d44410b325fee07866eb3163af8","sha":"4ca3691af6d41d44410b325fee07866eb3163af8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/4ca3691af6d41d44410b325fee07866eb3163af8"}],"sha":"3eb0812a597926a07cdf379e5813a25df50bd878","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/3eb0812a597926a07cdf379e5813a25df50bd878"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19351845?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pirut","id":19351845,"login":"pirut","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MzUxODQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/4ca3691af6d41d44410b325fee07866eb3163af8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T18:47:53Z","email":"scottbussardjr@gmail.com","name":"JR Bussard"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T18:47:53Z","email":"scottbussardjr@gmail.com","name":"JR Bussard"},"message":"Layer the world: foliage in front of you, haze behind\n\nDimming with distance made the picture recede, but it did not make a space\nyou are standing inside. That needs planes moving at different rates, so\nthere are now three: haze drifting behind the ground at 0.45x, the world\nitself, and foliage sliding in front at 1.55x — including in front of your\ncharacter, which is the part that actually sells being in the world rather\nthan looking down at it.\n\nThe near plane is clumped from a noise field rather than sprinkled per\ncell. Sprinkled, it read as static or a dirty lens; clumped, it reads as\nboughs with gaps between them.\n\nIt is also kept out of the middle of the frame. Depth is not worth having\nif it hides the square you are standing on, so density is zero within nine\ncells of the player and thickens toward the edges. The plane is blurred,\nbecause something close to the lens would be.\n\nBoth surfaces: the site''s overworld and the Commons.\n\nsrc/lib/terrain.js stays untouched, so the live Commons world and\neverything built in it is unaffected — this is a frontend-only change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bf0b820b75e411c9fb6a2d76d7a915ccf6c665cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/git/trees/bf0b820b75e411c9fb6a2d76d7a915ccf6c665cf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/git/commits/4ca3691af6d41d44410b325fee07866eb3163af8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19351845?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pirut","id":19351845,"login":"pirut","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MzUxODQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/pirut/jrbussard/commit/4ca3691af6d41d44410b325fee07866eb3163af8","node_id":"C_kwDOMtjVTdoAKDRjYTM2OTFhZjZkNDFkNDQ0MTBiMzI1ZmVlMDc4NjZlYjMxNjNhZjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/pirut/jrbussard/commit/14e7d3e41c917318716889369ce0ee78f3cf676e","sha":"14e7d3e41c917318716889369ce0ee78f3cf676e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/14e7d3e41c917318716889369ce0ee78f3cf676e"}],"sha":"4ca3691af6d41d44410b325fee07866eb3163af8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/4ca3691af6d41d44410b325fee07866eb3163af8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19351845?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pirut","id":19351845,"login":"pirut","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MzUxODQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/14e7d3e41c917318716889369ce0ee78f3cf676e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T18:35:13Z","email":"scottbussardjr@gmail.com","name":"JR Bussard"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T18:35:13Z","email":"scottbussardjr@gmail.com","name":"JR Bussard"},"message":"Give the world grain and depth instead of an even carpet\n\nTaking the cell texture, the landscape and the depth from rangedrifter''s art,\nand leaving the palette alone.\n\nGrain. Every cell of a kind rendered at exactly one colour, so a field of\ngrass was a repeating pattern rather than ground. Neighbouring cells now sit\na notch apart in brightness, from a hash of their coordinates so it is stable\nand never shimmers as the camera moves. Applied to the light level rather\nthan by mixing a colour per cell: levels are already quantised, so runs of\none colour still collapse into a single span. Doing it in colour space looked\nidentical and tripled the spans per row.\n\nDepth. The darkness floor was 0.16, which kept the far field plainly legible\neverywhere and flattened the picture — every part of the screen sat at much\nthe same brightness. Cells can now fall most of the way to the background,\nand the player''s light falls off squared rather than linear, so there is a\nbright pool around you and somewhere for the world to recede to.\n\nLandscape. Woods were a flat 14% per-cell chance, which gives the same\ndensity everywhere and reads as a sprinkle. They now grow from a noise field:\nthickets, thinning edges, and clearings where the ground cover goes bare.\n\nsrc/lib/terrain.js is deliberately untouched. It defines the live Commons\nworld people have built in, and changing it would move the ground under\neverything already standing there.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2d521c84cb359268deb87868215b1b1ac45ade5c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/git/trees/2d521c84cb359268deb87868215b1b1ac45ade5c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/git/commits/14e7d3e41c917318716889369ce0ee78f3cf676e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19351845?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pirut","id":19351845,"login":"pirut","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MzUxODQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/pirut/jrbussard/commit/14e7d3e41c917318716889369ce0ee78f3cf676e","node_id":"C_kwDOMtjVTdoAKDE0ZTdkM2U0MWM5MTczMTg3MTY4ODkzNjljZTBlZTc4ZjNjZjY3NmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/pirut/jrbussard/commit/006600ab031b673d9e3d7926e5556916cdb09e9b","sha":"006600ab031b673d9e3d7926e5556916cdb09e9b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/006600ab031b673d9e3d7926e5556916cdb09e9b"}],"sha":"14e7d3e41c917318716889369ce0ee78f3cf676e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/14e7d3e41c917318716889369ce0ee78f3cf676e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19351845?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pirut","id":19351845,"login":"pirut","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MzUxODQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/006600ab031b673d9e3d7926e5556916cdb09e9b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T13:53:03Z","email":"scottbussardjr@gmail.com","name":"JR Bussard"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T13:53:03Z","email":"scottbussardjr@gmail.com","name":"JR Bussard"},"message":"Fix the blank /commons: the client never referenced the new use mutation\n\nI added `use` on the server and called useMutation(api.use) without adding\nit to the client''s function map, so api.use was undefined. Convex threw on\nrender and /commons went blank in production. The rest of the site was\nunaffected, since only that route mounts the component.\n\nThe client names Convex functions as strings — Create React App refuses to\nimport the generated api from outside src/ — so nothing connects the two\nsides at build time. It compiled cleanly, the server mutation tested fine\nover HTTP, and the tests were green; the only thing that would have caught\nit was loading the page, which I did not do after that change.\n\nsrc/lib/convex.test.js now reads convex/world.ts and checks the two agree\nin both directions. Confirmed it fails on exactly this mistake.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3a76d159220023301b62cb5a1d02cbdc6347ac36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/git/trees/3a76d159220023301b62cb5a1d02cbdc6347ac36"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/git/commits/006600ab031b673d9e3d7926e5556916cdb09e9b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19351845?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pirut","id":19351845,"login":"pirut","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MzUxODQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/pirut/jrbussard/commit/006600ab031b673d9e3d7926e5556916cdb09e9b","node_id":"C_kwDOMtjVTdoAKDAwNjYwMGFiMDMxYjY3M2Q5ZTNkNzkyNmU1NTU2OTE2Y2RiMDllOWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/pirut/jrbussard/commit/8b2ced93eb1576121804dc83c7a200ae13200d3a","sha":"8b2ced93eb1576121804dc83c7a200ae13200d3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/8b2ced93eb1576121804dc83c7a200ae13200d3a"}],"sha":"006600ab031b673d9e3d7926e5556916cdb09e9b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/006600ab031b673d9e3d7926e5556916cdb09e9b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19351845?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pirut","id":19351845,"login":"pirut","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MzUxODQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/8b2ced93eb1576121804dc83c7a200ae13200d3a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T13:49:40Z","email":"scottbussardjr@gmail.com","name":"JR Bussard"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T13:49:40Z","email":"scottbussardjr@gmail.com","name":"JR Bussard"},"message":"Doors that open and shut, readable signs, and split mouse buttons\n\nDoors were decorative — always passable, with no way to work them. They now\ncarry an open/shut state: a shut one is solid, and blocks monsters too, so\nwalling a hut with a door in it finally does something. Anybody can swing a\ndoor, since doors are for getting through rather than for owning, but taking\none down still needs to be yours. It refuses to shut on someone standing in\nthe doorway. Open draws as '' and shut as +, the roguelike convention, and\nboth are ASCII so neither can fall back to a font of a different width.\n\nSigns stored their text and had no way to read it. Left-clicking one now\nreads it back with who wrote it, and the readout under the field shows the\ntext while it is selected.\n\nMouse buttons are split as asked: left works the world as it is — chop,\nmine, swing a door, read a sign — and right places the selected block.\nBoth go through the same handlers as g and b, so keyboard play is unchanged\nand the thumb pad keeps working where there is no right button.\n\nAlso fixed while here: the thumb pad''s G and B passed the click event\nstraight through as if it were a target cell.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"88bc15fa38b5f79d660e830d728fe0a34daa7e59","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/git/trees/88bc15fa38b5f79d660e830d728fe0a34daa7e59"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/git/commits/8b2ced93eb1576121804dc83c7a200ae13200d3a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19351845?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pirut","id":19351845,"login":"pirut","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MzUxODQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/pirut/jrbussard/commit/8b2ced93eb1576121804dc83c7a200ae13200d3a","node_id":"C_kwDOMtjVTdoAKDhiMmNlZDkzZWIxNTc2MTIxODA0ZGM4M2M3YTIwMGFlMTMyMDBkM2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/pirut/jrbussard/commit/1155986e16fe73ae297d778ed2e1b498c734e5e7","sha":"1155986e16fe73ae297d778ed2e1b498c734e5e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/1155986e16fe73ae297d778ed2e1b498c734e5e7"}],"sha":"8b2ced93eb1576121804dc83c7a200ae13200d3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/8b2ced93eb1576121804dc83c7a200ae13200d3a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19351845?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pirut","id":19351845,"login":"pirut","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MzUxODQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/1155986e16fe73ae297d778ed2e1b498c734e5e7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T13:20:12Z","email":"scottbussardjr@gmail.com","name":"JR Bussard"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T13:20:12Z","email":"scottbussardjr@gmail.com","name":"JR Bussard"},"message":"Point and click to build, within a reach radius\n\nBuilding a tile at a time by walking onto each square was tedious. You can\nnow click anywhere within 4 tiles: the hovered cell gets a selection box,\neverything in reach is lifted a little so the working area reads at a\nglance, and the box turns red outside it.\n\nA click does the obvious thing for what is under it — chop a tree, mine a\nrock, take back something you built, otherwise place the selected block —\nand the line under the field says which before you commit. The mouse takes\nover aiming while it is over the field; otherwise you still aim with the\ndirection you last walked, and g / b / x act on the same cell either way.\n\nREACH lives in src/lib/terrain.js beside the terrain generator, so the area\nthe browser offers is the same one the server enforces. The client only\ndecides what to offer: build, harvest and demolish all re-check reach\nserver-side, and building on top of another player is now refused too.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"729ebfdd62c4642b96d145f7773f135e0caa371c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/git/trees/729ebfdd62c4642b96d145f7773f135e0caa371c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/git/commits/1155986e16fe73ae297d778ed2e1b498c734e5e7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19351845?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pirut","id":19351845,"login":"pirut","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MzUxODQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/pirut/jrbussard/commit/1155986e16fe73ae297d778ed2e1b498c734e5e7","node_id":"C_kwDOMtjVTdoAKDExNTU5ODZlMTZmZTczYWUyOTdkNzc4ZWQyZTFiNDk4YzczNGU1ZTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/pirut/jrbussard/commit/91b237931bb62e5c7207f5ed092e51ab4f1d72a6","sha":"91b237931bb62e5c7207f5ed092e51ab4f1d72a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/91b237931bb62e5c7207f5ed092e51ab4f1d72a6"}],"sha":"1155986e16fe73ae297d778ed2e1b498c734e5e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/1155986e16fe73ae297d778ed2e1b498c734e5e7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19351845?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pirut","id":19351845,"login":"pirut","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MzUxODQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/91b237931bb62e5c7207f5ed092e51ab4f1d72a6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T13:03:17Z","email":"scottbussardjr@gmail.com","name":"JR Bussard"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T13:03:17Z","email":"scottbussardjr@gmail.com","name":"JR Bussard"},"message":"Let cleared ground be built on, and show what you are aiming at\n\nGathering was a dead end. build() tested the tile against tileAt(), which\ndescribes the generated landscape and never changes — a chopped tree still\nreads as TREE forever — so \"clear it first\" fired even on ground you had\njust cleared. Harvesting a tile made it permanently unbuildable, the exact\nopposite of the intent. What you did to the ground lives in the cells\noverlay, so a stump or rubble there now counts as cleared.\n\nThat also makes bridges work: a path laid on water is walkable, because\ncollision prefers the overlay''s solidity over the terrain underneath.\nVerified by walking the road to open water, building onto it, and crossing.\n\nBuilding was also hard to aim, since nothing showed which tile g / b / x\nwould act on. The faced cell is now drawn as a bright cursor and named\nunderneath — \"facing tree — g chops it for wood\", \"facing cleared ground —\nb builds here\", \"facing wall · someone — not yours to remove\". Walking into\nsomething you cannot pass still turns you, so that is how you aim. A path\nover water draws as a bridge rather than a path.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c27f3de4c11f1399d0c403700abc2fb0d6fb7b51","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/git/trees/c27f3de4c11f1399d0c403700abc2fb0d6fb7b51"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/git/commits/91b237931bb62e5c7207f5ed092e51ab4f1d72a6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19351845?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pirut","id":19351845,"login":"pirut","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MzUxODQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/pirut/jrbussard/commit/91b237931bb62e5c7207f5ed092e51ab4f1d72a6","node_id":"C_kwDOMtjVTdoAKDkxYjIzNzkzMWJiNjJlNWM3MjA3ZjVlZDA5MmU1MWFiNGYxZDcyYTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/pirut/jrbussard/commit/36fb7695fe470348d0f86581b3b157b0caa668b3","sha":"36fb7695fe470348d0f86581b3b157b0caa668b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/36fb7695fe470348d0f86581b3b157b0caa668b3"}],"sha":"91b237931bb62e5c7207f5ed092e51ab4f1d72a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/91b237931bb62e5c7207f5ed092e51ab4f1d72a6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19351845?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pirut","id":19351845,"login":"pirut","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MzUxODQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/36fb7695fe470348d0f86581b3b157b0caa668b3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T12:48:19Z","email":"scottbussardjr@gmail.com","name":"JR Bussard"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T12:48:19Z","email":"scottbussardjr@gmail.com","name":"JR Bussard"},"message":"Make the Foundry projects link again, and render the fields they gained\n\nWhen the project records grew status/since/highlights/links[], three render\nsites were left reaching for the old flat `project.href`: the Foundry panel,\nthe site index, and the screen-reader mirror. The Foundry panel put out an\nanchor with href={undefined} — the projects opened but went nowhere, which\nis what was reported.\n\nThe panel now renders the whole record: role · year · status in the meta\nline, highlights as a list, and every entry in links[] as its own action.\nThe other two take links[0].\n\nsrc/data/site.test.js guards the contract, since data and components were\nonly meeting at runtime and nothing caught the mismatch.\n\nConvex toolchain, continued: the earlier fix was right but incomplete — it\npinned typescript@^5 in package.json without node_modules being reinstalled,\nso the same 62 errors came back. Rather than leave that as a tripwire,\n`npm run commons` / `npm run commons:deploy` now run a preflight that checks\nthe installed TypeScript and prints one actionable line instead.\n\nChecked whether the pin could be avoided entirely by loosening the tsconfig\nto node resolution + ES2022: it cannot. Convex''s own shipped .d.ts files use\nTS5-only syntax that 4.9 cannot parse, and skipLibCheck does not help\nbecause those are syntax errors. That finding is recorded in the tsconfig.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f8caa4daa800368a3f7ef24f7fdaf518cd2dceab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/git/trees/f8caa4daa800368a3f7ef24f7fdaf518cd2dceab"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/git/commits/36fb7695fe470348d0f86581b3b157b0caa668b3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19351845?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pirut","id":19351845,"login":"pirut","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MzUxODQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/pirut/jrbussard/commit/36fb7695fe470348d0f86581b3b157b0caa668b3","node_id":"C_kwDOMtjVTdoAKDM2ZmI3Njk1ZmU0NzAzNDhkMGY4NjU4MWIzYjE1N2IwY2FhNjY4YjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/pirut/jrbussard/commit/1ac93077fc87081d1dcd0eec023f3c7105b34202","sha":"1ac93077fc87081d1dcd0eec023f3c7105b34202","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/1ac93077fc87081d1dcd0eec023f3c7105b34202"}],"sha":"36fb7695fe470348d0f86581b3b157b0caa668b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/36fb7695fe470348d0f86581b3b157b0caa668b3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19351845?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pirut","id":19351845,"login":"pirut","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MzUxODQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/1ac93077fc87081d1dcd0eec023f3c7105b34202/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T12:34:24Z","email":"scottbussardjr@gmail.com","name":"JR Bussard"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T12:34:24Z","email":"scottbussardjr@gmail.com","name":"JR Bussard"},"message":"Fix the install break from pinning TypeScript 5\n\nreact-scripts@5 declares peerOptional typescript \"^3.2.1 || ^4\", so adding\ntypescript@^5 for the Convex typecheck made `npm install` fail on Vercel\nwith ERESOLVE and the last two builds errored out. Production kept serving\nthe previous deployment, so the site stayed up.\n\nThe app is plain JavaScript and never invokes tsc — only the Convex\nfunctions need TypeScript — so the conflict is spurious. .npmrc sets\nlegacy-peer-deps so local and CI resolve identically, and the lockfile is\nregenerated to match.\n\nVerified by reproducing Vercel''s clean `npm install` from just\npackage.json + lock + .npmrc in an empty directory: 1440 packages, exit 0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"19861273734cd63f5f8b4463ac20232b6402d486","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/git/trees/19861273734cd63f5f8b4463ac20232b6402d486"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/git/commits/1ac93077fc87081d1dcd0eec023f3c7105b34202","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19351845?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pirut","id":19351845,"login":"pirut","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MzUxODQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/pirut/jrbussard/commit/1ac93077fc87081d1dcd0eec023f3c7105b34202","node_id":"C_kwDOMtjVTdoAKDFhYzkzMDc3ZmM4NzA4MWQxZGNkMGVlYzAyM2YzYzcxMDViMzQyMDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/pirut/jrbussard/commit/7df7a90d57f59818895d76a25a25912adf5e681f","sha":"7df7a90d57f59818895d76a25a25912adf5e681f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/7df7a90d57f59818895d76a25a25912adf5e681f"}],"sha":"1ac93077fc87081d1dcd0eec023f3c7105b34202","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/1ac93077fc87081d1dcd0eec023f3c7105b34202"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19351845?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pirut","id":19351845,"login":"pirut","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MzUxODQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/7df7a90d57f59818895d76a25a25912adf5e681f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T12:23:03Z","email":"scottbussardjr@gmail.com","name":"JR Bussard"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T12:23:03Z","email":"scottbussardjr@gmail.com","name":"JR Bussard"},"message":"Keep .env.example out of the blanket .env* ignore\n\nvercel link appended .env*, which would hide the template documenting how\nto link an existing Convex project.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c664c634141ec1e2d682c156bf1371454c2cdaaf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/git/trees/c664c634141ec1e2d682c156bf1371454c2cdaaf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/git/commits/7df7a90d57f59818895d76a25a25912adf5e681f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19351845?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pirut","id":19351845,"login":"pirut","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MzUxODQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/pirut/jrbussard/commit/7df7a90d57f59818895d76a25a25912adf5e681f","node_id":"C_kwDOMtjVTdoAKDdkZjdhOTBkNTdmNTk4MTg4OTVkNzZhMjVhMjU5MTJhZGY1ZTY4MWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/pirut/jrbussard/commit/d2b960caf9ca752ffae214199090318113f735f2","sha":"d2b960caf9ca752ffae214199090318113f735f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/d2b960caf9ca752ffae214199090318113f735f2"}],"sha":"7df7a90d57f59818895d76a25a25912adf5e681f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/7df7a90d57f59818895d76a25a25912adf5e681f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19351845?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pirut","id":19351845,"login":"pirut","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MzUxODQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/d2b960caf9ca752ffae214199090318113f735f2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T12:22:20Z","email":"scottbussardjr@gmail.com","name":"JR Bussard"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T12:22:20Z","email":"scottbussardjr@gmail.com","name":"JR Bussard"},"message":"Keep the character grid square when fonts lack a glyph\n\nThe art is only aligned while every glyph is exactly one cell wide. That\nholds for ASCII in any monospace font, but not for the box drawing, block\nand symbol characters the world is drawn with: if the local font lacks\none, the browser substitutes a face with a different advance width and\nthe row shifts. A few symbols (☺ ★ ▲) can also be given emoji\npresentation, which is double width. Which characters break depends\nentirely on the platform''s fonts, so it looked fine here and broken\nelsewhere.\n\nRather than guess which glyphs are safe on Windows, Linux and Android,\neverything outside printable ASCII now goes out wrapped in an element\npinned to exactly 1ch, so substitution can happen and the grid still\nholds. ASCII stays as bare text, keeping the run-grouping fast path.\n\nMeasured under a forced proportional substitution: unpinned, the cells\nrendered at five different widths between 7.3px and 18.6px; pinned, all\n1246 of them are exactly one column.\n\nAlso drops U+223C from the water animation — it is missing from several\ncommon monospace fonts and was the most visible offender.\n\nConvex developer setup, from a report of `npx convex dev` failing:\n\n- Pin typescript@^5 as a devDependency. Convex''s tsconfig needs\n  \"Bundler\" module resolution and the ES2023 lib; the repo was resolving\n  TypeScript 4.9.5 transitively, which produced 62 typecheck errors.\n- Check convex/tsconfig.json in rather than letting Convex generate it,\n  so every machine typechecks identically.\n- Document in .env.example and the README that a fresh clone has no\n  .env.local, so plain `npx convex dev` creates a NEW project instead of\n  using this one — link with --configure existing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9e49efb9e31a1e6bd87b8f70d5f780acd231b805","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/git/trees/9e49efb9e31a1e6bd87b8f70d5f780acd231b805"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/git/commits/d2b960caf9ca752ffae214199090318113f735f2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19351845?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pirut","id":19351845,"login":"pirut","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MzUxODQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/pirut/jrbussard/commit/d2b960caf9ca752ffae214199090318113f735f2","node_id":"C_kwDOMtjVTdoAKGQyYjk2MGNhZjljYTc1MmZmYWUyMTQxOTkwOTAzMTgxMTNmNzM1ZjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/pirut/jrbussard/commit/76212c2cfa2f9d9afe84f23dc0c317aa2f1ea1b8","sha":"76212c2cfa2f9d9afe84f23dc0c317aa2f1ea1b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/76212c2cfa2f9d9afe84f23dc0c317aa2f1ea1b8"}],"sha":"d2b960caf9ca752ffae214199090318113f735f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/d2b960caf9ca752ffae214199090318113f735f2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19351845?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pirut","id":19351845,"login":"pirut","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MzUxODQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/76212c2cfa2f9d9afe84f23dc0c317aa2f1ea1b8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T12:10:37Z","email":"scottbussardjr@gmail.com","name":"JR Bussard"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T12:10:37Z","email":"scottbussardjr@gmail.com","name":"JR Bussard"},"message":"Document the split deploy: git push ships the site, convex deploy ships the backend\n\nThe two halves deploy separately, which is easy to trip over — changing\nsrc/lib/terrain.js and only pushing would leave the browser and server\ndisagreeing about what is solid.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6be4576faf710a0ab364d7b5331cc42836c7abbe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/git/trees/6be4576faf710a0ab364d7b5331cc42836c7abbe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/git/commits/76212c2cfa2f9d9afe84f23dc0c317aa2f1ea1b8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19351845?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pirut","id":19351845,"login":"pirut","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MzUxODQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/pirut/jrbussard/commit/76212c2cfa2f9d9afe84f23dc0c317aa2f1ea1b8","node_id":"C_kwDOMtjVTdoAKDc2MjEyYzJjZmEyZjlkOWFmZTg0ZjIzZGMwYzMxN2FhMmYxZWExYjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/pirut/jrbussard/commit/820b47c81d6d03397eac822dc1ad09fc67d1a375","sha":"820b47c81d6d03397eac822dc1ad09fc67d1a375","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/820b47c81d6d03397eac822dc1ad09fc67d1a375"}],"sha":"76212c2cfa2f9d9afe84f23dc0c317aa2f1ea1b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/76212c2cfa2f9d9afe84f23dc0c317aa2f1ea1b8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19351845?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pirut","id":19351845,"login":"pirut","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MzUxODQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/820b47c81d6d03397eac822dc1ad09fc67d1a375/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T17:12:17Z","email":"scottbussardjr@gmail.com","name":"JR Bussard"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T17:12:17Z","email":"scottbussardjr@gmail.com","name":"JR Bussard"},"message":"Add a multiplayer sandbox, three more games, and richer rooms\n\nEach room of the world got a functional pass, and the Arcade got real\nthings to play.\n\nThe Commons — a genuine MMO on Convex (chosen for reactive queries: a\nmutation lands and every connected client re-renders, no websocket code):\n\n- Endless world. No map is stored; every tile is a pure function of its\n  coordinates. src/lib/terrain.js is imported by BOTH the browser and the\n  Convex functions, so client and server can never disagree and no terrain\n  crosses the wire. Roads run out from the origin forever so you can always\n  walk home. Entities are chunk-indexed, so querying one corner never scans\n  the rest.\n- Server-authoritative movement, building and combat, all rate-limited.\n- Sandbox: chop and mine for wood and stone, build walls, paths, doors,\n  torches and signs. Buildings persist for everyone; you can only demolish\n  your own; torches keep monsters back.\n- Dynamic: twelve-minute day/night, rolling weather, terrain that regrows.\n- Chat with speech bubbles over the speaker, per-name colours, and\n  /me /who /where /home /help.\n- The tick loop parks itself when nobody is on the field, so an idle world\n  costs nothing to keep open.\n\nPlay-testing the server found four real bugs, all fixed: players spawned\nstacked on one tile; monsters camped the spawn and killed idle players;\na pack of three deleted a new arrival in about two seconds (each monster\nnow has a swing timer and a player can only be hurt once per second); and\nsending a chat message left focus in the input so WASD silently stopped\nworking.\n\nAlso in the arcade: SNAKE, BREAKOUT, and THE NIGHT SHIFT, an idle\noperations game that keeps earning while you are away.\n\nRoom-by-room improvements:\n\n- Library: card-catalog terminal listing every note, prev/next paging\n  between notes, hearth and reading room.\n- Observatory: commit-log terminal wired to the GitHub activity that was\n  being fetched and never shown; repos are now curated (pinned first, no\n  forks or empty repos) instead of whatever the API returned first.\n- Foundry: projects carry status, year, highlights and multiple links;\n  machines rebuilt with chimneys and a furnace.\n- Atrium: noticeboard terminal with the latest note and push; features\n  moved into quadrants so the crossing stays clear.\n- Arcade: six cabinets; beacon: a railed pier over open water.\n- Every room now has its own tint and ambient light level.\n\nTests cover the terrain contract the two sides share, plus the existing\nmap-walkability checks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4c39cb572fb1cc4333dbb010a0ae4601a5b74e17","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/git/trees/4c39cb572fb1cc4333dbb010a0ae4601a5b74e17"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/git/commits/820b47c81d6d03397eac822dc1ad09fc67d1a375","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19351845?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pirut","id":19351845,"login":"pirut","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MzUxODQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/pirut/jrbussard/commit/820b47c81d6d03397eac822dc1ad09fc67d1a375","node_id":"C_kwDOMtjVTdoAKDgyMGI0N2M4MWQ2ZDAzMzk3ZWFjODIyZGMxYWQwOWZjNjdkMWEzNzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/pirut/jrbussard/commit/7fd8b9ae471e6a5425932803173493b122e000dc","sha":"7fd8b9ae471e6a5425932803173493b122e000dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/7fd8b9ae471e6a5425932803173493b122e000dc"}],"sha":"820b47c81d6d03397eac822dc1ad09fc67d1a375","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/820b47c81d6d03397eac822dc1ad09fc67d1a375"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19351845?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pirut","id":19351845,"login":"pirut","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MzUxODQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/commits/7fd8b9ae471e6a5425932803173493b122e000dc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T15:15:53Z","email":"scottbussardjr@gmail.com","name":"JR Bussard"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T15:15:53Z","email":"scottbussardjr@gmail.com","name":"JR Bussard"},"message":"Replace the portfolio with an explorable ASCII world\n\nThe site is now a character grid you walk around as `@`. Six rooms off a\ncentral atrium: the Library (Sanity notes, one per shelf slot), the Foundry\n(projects), the Observatory (live GitHub repos), the Arcade (small projects\nhosted here), and the Beacon (contact). Stand next to a prop and press E.\n\n- src/world/ holds the engine: rooms are authored as plain ASCII, stamped\n  into a tile grid, walls auto-tile, and a lighting pass dims by distance\n  from the player and the torches.\n- Props whose slot has no content behind it render cold and inert, so an\n  empty shelf or an unplugged cabinet reads as empty rather than broken.\n- microfrontends/registry.js is the single place to add a hosted project:\n  one entry registers the route, lights the next cabinet, and lists it in\n  the index.\n- Keyboard, thumb pad on touch, an `index` panel of plain links, and a\n  screen-reader mirror of all content for anyone who would rather not walk.\n- Tests assert the map stays walkable: every room reachable from spawn,\n  every prop approachable, atrium lanes clear, and room labels not colliding.\n\nDeletes the old scrolling portfolio and the pre-React static pages.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0208b7bf7588cf05e0a92732dada96cd78e41e94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/git/trees/0208b7bf7588cf05e0a92732dada96cd78e41e94"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pirut/jrbussard/git/commits/7fd8b9ae471e6a5425932803173493b122e000dc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19351845?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pirut/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pirut","id":19351845,"login":"pirut","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MzU