/konstructio/konstruct-ui/git/commits/6fa91bd3b0aabbcd9c4606366f430b06729279ab","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173219915?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konstruct-bot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konstruct-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konstruct-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konstruct-bot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/konstruct-bot","id":173219915,"login":"konstruct-bot","node_id":"U_kgDOClMgSw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konstruct-bot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konstruct-bot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konstruct-bot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konstruct-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konstruct-bot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konstruct-bot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/konstructio/konstruct-ui/commit/6fa91bd3b0aabbcd9c4606366f430b06729279ab","node_id":"C_kwDOM3rbOdoAKDZmYTkxYmQzYjBhYWJiY2Q5YzQ2MDYzNjZmNDMwYjA2NzI5Mjc5YWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/konstructio/konstruct-ui/commit/372e9f9c9475657c2028fec5a7bbf8212bc0dd84","sha":"372e9f9c9475657c2028fec5a7bbf8212bc0dd84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konstructio/konstruct-ui/commits/372e9f9c9475657c2028fec5a7bbf8212bc0dd84"}],"sha":"6fa91bd3b0aabbcd9c4606366f430b06729279ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konstructio/konstruct-ui/commits/6fa91bd3b0aabbcd9c4606366f430b06729279ab"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7634296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/futjesus","id":7634296,"login":"futjesus","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2MzQyOTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konstructio/konstruct-ui/commits/372e9f9c9475657c2028fec5a7bbf8212bc0dd84/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T18:05:58Z","email":"futjesus@gmail.com","name":"Jesús Manuel Fuentes Trejo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T18:05:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"✨ feat(toast): stacked toast queue with a built-in store, provider-less usage and dark mode (#749)\n\n* ✨ feat(toast): stacked toast queue with a built-in store, provider-less usage and dark mode\n\nReplaces the Radix single-toast `Toast` (unused by any consumer) with a bottom-right stack: the newest toast sits in front, older ones peek behind it, and hovering or focusing the stack expands it into a list. Timers hold while expanded and either resume with the time left (default) or restart from the full duration and dismiss one by one, oldest first (`hoverBehavior=\"restart\"`). The window losing focus counts as leaving the stack, so toasts never get stuck behind a pointer left over them.\n\nState lives in the library: `createToastStore` is a dependency-free store (`getState`/`subscribe`, zustand-compatible surface) with a default duration of 3 s and a queue limit of 5. `<Toast />` works on its own, configuring the built-in store through `duration` and `limit`, and `useToast()` publishes into it from anywhere; `ToastProvider` is optional, to scope a subtree or inject a store shared with other code. Passing `toasts` and `onDismiss` keeps the stack fully controlled.\n\nVisuals follow the Figma toast in both modes. Dark mode composes the 10% tint over an opaque `metal-950` base so page content never bleeds through; the border is drawn as an inset ring on the clipped `li`, which keeps it visible on compressed cards and avoids the 2 px snap `box-content` caused when `motion` settled `height: auto`. Cards size to their content up to 390 px. With a description the title drops to 14 px and the icon to 20 px so both sit on one line; compressed cards fold the description with opacity only, so measured heights stay natural and every card animates to its expanded position at once. Springs replace the fixed easing and `will-change: transform` keeps each card on a stable compositor layer, removing the 1 px text jump at the end of the animation.\n\n`useIsHydrated` becomes a public hook so the portal renders nothing during SSR and hydration. The `variant` prop is renamed to `type`, matching `Alert` and the payload other apps already send.\n\n* ⬆️ chore: update dependencies\n\nNon-interactive `npm-check-updates --format group -u` run honouring `.ncurc.json` (eslint, typescript and @tanstack/react-table stay rejected). Patch and minor bumps only: Storybook 10.6.1, Vitest 5.0.3 with its coverage plugin, Vite 8.3.1, vite-plugin-dts 5.1.1, jsdom 30.1.1, typescript-eslint 8.71, @types/react 19.3, react-query 5.104, react-virtual 3.14.13, react-day-picker 10.0.2, lucide-react 1.49, motion 13.4.6, tailwind-merge 3.7, autoprefixer 10.6.1, google-libphonenumber 3.2.47, prettier 3.9.9 and eslint-plugin-react-refresh 0.5.7.\n\nThe `@tanstack/react-query` peer range moves to ^5.104 to match the version built and tested against. Lockfile regenerated from scratch and verified with `npm ci` on linux/amd64 (node:24) so the `@emnapi/*` optional entries survive for the Linux runners.","tree":{"sha":"45109a5857acf6e58734122dc33142b619c10274","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konstructio/konstruct-ui/git/trees/45109a5857acf6e58734122dc33142b619c10274"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konstructio/konstruct-ui/git/commits/372e9f9c9475657c2028fec5a7bbf8212bc0dd84","verification":{"payload":"tree 45109a5857acf6e58734122dc33142b619c10274\nparent f406ba1826d048f8366c30455119af7905403f37\nauthor Jesús Manuel Fuentes Trejo <futjesus@gmail.com> 1790791558 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790791558 -0300\n\n✨ feat(toast): stacked toast queue with a built-in store, provider-less usage and dark mode (#749)\n\n* ✨ feat(toast): stacked toast queue with a built-in store, provider-less usage and dark mode\n\nReplaces the Radix single-toast `Toast` (unused by any consumer) with a bottom-right stack: the newest toast sits in front, older ones peek behind it, and hovering or focusing the stack expands it into a list. Timers hold while expanded and either resume with the time left (default) or restart from the full duration and dismiss one by one, oldest first (`hoverBehavior=\"restart\"`). The window losing focus counts as leaving the stack, so toasts never get stuck behind a pointer left over them.\n\nState lives in the library: `createToastStore` is a dependency-free store (`getState`/`subscribe`, zustand-compatible surface) with a default duration of 3 s and a queue limit of 5. `<Toast />` works on its own, configuring the built-in store through `duration` and `limit`, and `useToast()` publishes into it from anywhere; `ToastProvider` is optional, to scope a subtree or inject a store shared with other code. Passing `toasts` and `onDismiss` keeps the stack fully controlled.\n\nVisuals follow the Figma toast in both modes. Dark mode composes the 10% tint over an opaque `metal-950` base so page content never bleeds through; the border is drawn as an inset ring on the clipped `li`, which keeps it visible on compressed cards and avoids the 2 px snap `box-content` caused when `motion` settled `height: auto`. Cards size to their content up to 390 px. With a description the title drops to 14 px and the icon to 20 px so both sit on one line; compressed cards fold the description with opacity only, so measured heights stay natural and every card animates to its expanded position at once. Springs replace the fixed easing and `will-change: transform` keeps each card on a stable compositor layer, removing the 1 px text jump at the end of the animation.\n\n`useIsHydrated` becomes a public hook so the portal renders nothing during SSR and hydration. The `variant` prop is renamed to `type`, matching `Alert` and the payload other apps already send.\n\n* ⬆️ chore: update dependencies\n\nNon-interactive `npm-check-updates --format group -u` run honouring `.ncurc.json` (eslint, typescript and @tanstack/react-table stay rejected). Patch and minor bumps only: Storybook 10.6.1, Vitest 5.0.3 with its coverage plugin, Vite 8.3.1, vite-plugin-dts 5.1.1, jsdom 30.1.1, typescript-eslint 8.71, @types/react 19.3, react-query 5.104, react-virtual 3.14.13, react-day-picker 10.0.2, lucide-react 1.49, motion 13.4.6, tailwind-merge 3.7, autoprefixer 10.6.1, google-libphonenumber 3.2.47, prettier 3.9.9 and eslint-plugin-react-refresh 0.5.7.\n\nThe `@tanstack/react-query` peer range moves to ^5.104 to match the version built and tested against. Lockfile regenerated from scratch and verified with `npm ci` on linux/amd64 (node:24) so the `@emnapi/*` optional entries survive for the Linux runners.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvU+GCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARcoQACNi/ytmUrGN+aOXKatIBlz/\nilSjQeyi2/ZWo8vwgESHeCRR/R8DP5cbvOZd5SHVLqpHcoM3uNPymFphRpoLuObd\nh+percsNW3JsZTw+Lw6AZWl4ojYvcH0LMlRzqVAaIKaNANYCTX2mHygOVJw2hpEM\nTV1A7TM6UmE5/g8x/cLZFkWeGUa25JxW0nhUC2sjQcNGOgReftQPCWcAZaRU4kSg\ngTq3UOo