count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T20:27:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"✨ feat: add isPortal and onValueChange to Select (#718)\n\n`isPortal` renders the options list in a portal positioned with Radix\nPopover (the same mechanism the table page-size dropdown uses), so the\nlist is no longer clipped by `overflow` containers such as drawers, modals\nor table cells. Kubernetes rewrote the whole component as PortalSelect for\nthis, without keyboard navigation. Click-outside and focusout detection\nnow treat the portaled list as inside the select, so selecting an option\nor moving focus into the list does not close it. `portalClassName` lets\nconsumers raise the z-index above custom overlays.\n\n`onValueChange(value)` complements the event-shaped `onChange`; every\nmicrofrontend wrote the same adapter to bridge Select into\nreact-hook-form (billing CountrySelect, settings TimezoneSelect, ...).\n\n`useClickOutside` accepts an array of refs so a component with a portaled\npart can declare several \"inside\" roots.","tree":{"sha":"bf32e15586214806a8bd9d6008e99ecee0cced12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konstructio/konstruct-ui/git/trees/bf32e15586214806a8bd9d6008e99ecee0cced12"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konstructio/konstruct-ui/git/commits/fa65b288f7290655ca679dfe3f3bb67a85c93323","verification":{"payload":"tree bf32e15586214806a8bd9d6008e99ecee0cced12\nparent 1367c3c5128abe07cf731115e9eed511bd5d1bc0\nauthor Jesús Manuel Fuentes Trejo <futjesus@gmail.com> 1788467266 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788467266 -0400\n\n✨ feat: add isPortal and onValueChange to Select (#718)\n\n`isPortal` renders the options list in a portal positioned with Radix\nPopover (the same mechanism the table page-size dropdown uses), so the\nlist is no longer clipped by `overflow` containers such as drawers, modals\nor table cells. Kubernetes rewrote the whole component as PortalSelect for\nthis, without keyboard navigation. Click-outside and focusout detection\nnow treat the portaled list as inside the select, so selecting an option\nor moving focus into the list does not close it. `portalClassName` lets\nconsumers raise the z-index above custom overlays.\n\n`onValueChange(value)` complements the event-shaped `onChange`; every\nmicrofrontend wrote the same adapter to bridge Select into\nreact-hook-form (billing CountrySelect, settings TimezoneSelect, ...).\n\n`useClickOutside` accepts an array of refs so a component with a portaled\npart can declare several \"inside\" roots.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmdhCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdMIQAC8XBEy7q1e+3f03d3D9T5Zk\nPWR8fe+l/WuQCqZKPDTpdUAa4YpgnOvAulc5wpCAQjq3PXRNyRzC228RgK4oN3nV\nd20NNn58FYjMFismNnC8ex0y/7ptIbxPoAcG3J/A6iYL/XQ2eTs0pv2tu+IVTSkM\nheJB+kaAigVuL5V3ih8Fj+IEHX60GAmSdx2YofVB8ZLPSWnI/syYcHd2IufmPJss\nKYocaY36dd5tJFieamQnShDCGX31zVR0ctIuR5sz2voCwnDB2d+wekKisyF3ahfu\n1Ux56mLSfyIhPDmyUSV/cbSwBu0KfOMlt2fDTpjO9GApJ3bt8Ks3z251kbD4UDm3\nCpOOO0JJMYx5/uK5JcAA52bSNuyiF6jKtJvoj+dhx7sG7nggGLuVTrOM4IhU2lsk\npjl5U+YKxbvi/hiXdfkoyX8aDqIilPVv2cAHytzVgwmnX4aBf4d9ICsoeV0/Wufa\nFJoHHi2tTbXUCnrPcJggx6jVbT6toX6VrOQFtXhImaJ5c+Vy+huJBlgqHBIC1msp\n0S2dVyGkytSvqWwrSlozMgAXjpvDROAVxQfN0yCPGPOLEp+WR6vzDJeobEOxMPiF\n2+NwhrmeCsSaipVmap3ReCeN7zylc83hJmnHg/6MhskC53+iBkpnyeYBr0qtMVIG\nGTr/xNRFMWJc65Z7m0UR\n=6bjj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-03T20:27:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/konstructio/konstruct-ui/commit/fa65b288f7290655ca679dfe3f3bb67a85c93323","node_id":"C_kwDOM3rbOdoAKGZhNjViMjg4ZjcyOTA2NTVjYTY3OWRmZTNmM2JiNjdhODVjOTMzMjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/konstructio/konstruct-ui/commit/1367c3c5128abe07cf731115e9eed511bd5d1bc0","sha":"1367c3c5128abe07cf731115e9eed511bd5d1bc0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konstructio/konstruct-ui/commits/1367c3c5128abe07cf731115e9eed511bd5d1bc0"}],"sha":"fa65b288f7290655ca679dfe3f3bb67a85c93323","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konstructio/konstruct-ui/commits/fa65b288f7290655ca679dfe3f3bb67a85c93323"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7634296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/futjesus","id":7634296,"login":"futjesus","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2MzQyOTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konstructio/konstruct-ui/commits/1367c3c5128abe07cf731115e9eed511bd5d1bc0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T20:27:11Z","email":"futjesus@gmail.com","name":"Jesús Manuel Fuentes Trejo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T20:27:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"🐛 fix: date inputs autofill off by default and a whole-pixel actions menu (#735)\n\n* 🐛 fix: keep browser autofill off the date range inputs\n\nThe From/To fields are plain text inputs, so the browser offered its own\nautofill list over the calendar panel — a dropdown of unrelated saved values\ncovering the days the user was about to click.\n\n`autoComplete=\"off\"` on both fields, plus a test asserting the attribute is\nthere, since nothing else in the render would reveal its loss.\n\n* 🐛 fix: snap the portalled actions menu to whole pixels\n\nA trigger whose right edge sits on a half pixel — table layouts routinely\nproduce one — placed the menu at x.5. The text inside it is then rasterized\ntwice: once on the compositing layer the enter animation''s transform creates,\nand once against the page grid after that transform is gone. The two roundings\ndisagree, so the labels appear to jump a pixel sideways as the menu settles.\n\nRounding `top` and `left` keeps the panel on the pixel grid, so both paints\nland on the same glyph positions. Layout was never moving, which is why no\npositional assertion caught it.\n\n* ✨ feat: let consumers choose the date inputs'' autofill\n\nTurning the browser''s autofill off is right for a picker sitting in a dropdown,\nwhere the saved-value list covers the calendar, but not a decision to make for\nevery consumer: a picker inside a form may want autofill.\n\n`autoComplete` now rides from `DateRangePicker` down to both date fields and\ndefaults to `''off''`, so the dropdown case stays fixed with nothing to pass and a\nform can opt back in.","tree":{"sha":"04524cb38723ce539c828d02eef43cfb0061bde2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konstructio/konstruct-ui/git/trees/04524cb38723ce539c828d02eef43cfb0061bde2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konstructio/konstruct-ui/git/commits/1367c3c5128abe07cf731115e9eed511bd5d1bc0","verification":{"payload":"tree 04524cb38723ce539c828d02eef43cfb0061bde2\nparent 820f7e87c3f77f4d223c2e9277292c2ce3f57cc4\nauthor Jesús Manuel Fuentes Trejo <futjesus@gmail.com> 1788467231 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788467231 -0400\n\n🐛 fix: date inputs autofill off by default and a whole-pixel actions menu (#735)\n\n* 🐛 fix: keep browser autofill off the date range inputs\n\nThe From/To fields are plain text inputs, so the browser offered its own\nautofill list over the calendar panel — a dropdown of unrelated saved values\ncovering the days the user was about to click.\n\n`autoComplete=\"off\"` on both fields, plus a test asserting the attribute is\nthere, since nothing else in the render would reveal its loss.\n\n* 🐛 fix: snap the portalled actions menu to whole pixels\n\nA trigger whose right edge sits on a half pixel — table layouts routinely\nproduce one — placed the menu at x.5. The text inside it is then rasterized\ntwice: once on the compositing layer the enter animation''s transform creates,\nand once against the page grid after that transform is gone. The two roundings\ndisagree, so the labels appear to jump a pixel sideways as the menu settles.\n\nRounding `top` and `left` keeps the panel on the pixel grid, so both paints\nland on the same glyph positions. Layout was never moving, which is why no\npositional assertion caught it.\n\n* ✨ feat: let consumers choose the date inputs'' autofill\n\nTurning the browser''s autofill off is right for a picker sitting in a dropdown,\nwhere the saved-value list covers the calendar, but not a decision to make for\nevery consumer: a picker inside a form may want autofill.\n\n`autoComplete` now rides from `DateRangePicker` down to both date fields and\ndefaults to `''off''`, so the dropdown case stays fixed with nothing to pass and a\nform can opt back in.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmdgfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsbUQAKwuP8jIvFvW29bLcuVX8FBF\ncFaw9E2PCYbHpoD9xPOK+l78llJ101sOLEkt6gAgLIYmNr0SKdHi6p2e3aWfRuE0\nQ3Vr6yvnrR5W1qqVa2V8+kLn72omfAtnWWzkSvoGRQaKeJaD+DlZslDO6XUxCO7k\nt1J2n9YKuBpkilPcevPxnFkwIjskr+6l/v0PAnuXflENvLT3o/kov96kwaWjqJMW\nfzK4QKQMikhiRvioVteXoI1z71zFYt39yg95GiPCqQmO12NKpSo6CVWZ0+g/vgo2\n0GAMHNJUBUAPSJ2UlszGMaCb4/JA++Cdz76EvS8Pw++M17r7e+tzCTkRTzQAcAzW\ny291H/6A+sv5h+UXC2P/IupvKJnVf/kbUVFIRw2wTL5yz0k3dotKQkdP4fETOdqq\nq9WR66DztaUWPiorWNib2VVUfcpNnyRcgc9PK4I5jiWCy/A0usVG7GM6OQAr4mCb\n1zipuZO1ZTr8/38YMJDCt7UCJfgmz1RdjElsVTHAXSzb10ylhzFAAg+AXbbx157Z\nNWV3sb72mw/LOjRBE1ELyzuHq4oK14XSKssmUflFgUGdb8+tG6opHTLRFeUv4caU\nwlvVqbq6IVbtLBYzp0xI/zTHFpuWBweeq12NjBrFudgCfXu289Zp/KSLikFlLczn\nmSBWF++m4aQSZiXobwFM\n=iAs6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-03T20:27:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/konstructio/konstruct-ui/commit/1367c3c5128a