e_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/konstructio/konstruct-ui/commit/30f55c5487c033f4a71882ee5d4e1ced74378818","node_id":"C_kwDOM3rbOdoAKDMwZjU1YzU0ODdjMDMzZjRhNzE4ODJlZTVkNGUxY2VkNzQzNzg4MTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/konstructio/konstruct-ui/commit/4a893753ac43853e5f421aa114589bc961d1f651","sha":"4a893753ac43853e5f421aa114589bc961d1f651","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konstructio/konstruct-ui/commits/4a893753ac43853e5f421aa114589bc961d1f651"}],"sha":"30f55c5487c033f4a71882ee5d4e1ced74378818","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konstructio/konstruct-ui/commits/30f55c5487c033f4a71882ee5d4e1ced74378818"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14883029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CristhianF7/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CristhianF7/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CristhianF7/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CristhianF7/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/CristhianF7","id":14883029,"login":"CristhianF7","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODgzMDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CristhianF7/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CristhianF7/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CristhianF7/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CristhianF7/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CristhianF7/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CristhianF7","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konstructio/konstruct-ui/commits/4a893753ac43853e5f421aa114589bc961d1f651/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T15:59:21Z","email":"CristhianF7@gmail.com","name":"Cristhian Fernández"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-24T15:59:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"🐛 fix: accessible names, error state and listbox semantics for composite controls (#702)\n\nApplies the same pass as the text-field fix to the controls built out of\nwrappers and popups, where the defects were mostly dangling id\nreferences rather than missing attributes.\n\nSelect gave its label and its combobox the same id:\n\n  <label id={m} htmlFor={m}>{label}</label>\n  <div id={m} role=\"combobox\" aria-labelledby={m} />\n\nMeasured on a labelled, required Select with an error: a duplicate id in\nthe document, `htmlFor` resolving to the label itself, `aria-labelledby`\nlanding on the label only by luck of document order, and no accessible\nname at all when `label` was omitted. Split into `-label` / `-control` /\n`-listbox` ids with an `aria-label={placeholder}` fallback.\n\nTimePicker used one identifier for four unrelated jobs — the label''s\n`htmlFor`, the control''s `aria-label`, and the hidden input''s `name` —\nwhile nothing carried it as an id. The control''s accessible name was\ntherefore the raw form name string: `<TimePicker name=\"startTime\" />`\nannounced as \"startTime\". Alongside that, `aria-expanded` was hardcoded\nto \"true\" so the trigger always reported itself as expanded,\n`aria-controls` referenced an id nothing carried, the hidden input\nsubmitted under the label id rather than `name`, and in select mode the\n`error` prop rendered nothing at all because the message lived inside the\ninput-mode branch.\n\nButtonGroup''s radiogroup had no accessible name: the label used\n`htmlFor` toward a `<div>`, which is not labelable, and the group''s\n`aria-labelledby` referenced an id nothing carried.\n\nAcross Select, PhoneNumberInput, TimePicker, ButtonGroup and ImageUpload:\nerror messages and helper text now carry ids referenced by\n`aria-describedby`, controls carry `aria-invalid`, and `isRequired` sets\n`aria-required` with the asterisk marked `aria-hidden` so it stays out of\nthe accessible name (WCAG 3.3.1). PhoneNumberInput also carried its own\ncopy of the Input `error.length >= 0` bug, treating `error=\"\"` as an\nerror state.\n\nTwo behaviour fixes surfaced by the above:\n\n- PhoneNumberInput dropped its own masking handler whenever a caller\n  passed `onChange`, because `{...delegated}` was spread after it. The\n  two are now composed.\n- DateRangePicker changes are required by the TimePicker fix and cannot\n  be split out: it renders its own label with no `htmlFor` and passed\n  `name=\"start time\"` so the buggy `aria-label` would name the field. It\n  now gets `id` and `ariaLabel` props to associate and name the control,\n  and an `ariaLabelTime` prop, because its two time fields share the\n  visible label \"Time\" and became mutually ambiguous once the form name\n  stopped disambiguating them. Visible design is unchanged.\n\nSelect listbox structure, the safe part of the combobox work:\n\n- Grouped options were rendered as a flat sibling list with the group\n  name in an `aria-hidden` `<li>`. Sighted users saw the grouping;\n  screen-reader users got an undifferentiated list. Options are now\n  wrapped in `<ul role=\"group\" aria-label={groupLabel}>`, so the tree\n  reads `listbox > group \"Europe\" > option`. Verified in a real render\n  that the nested list inherits `padding-inline-start: 0` and every row\n  keeps the same left offset and width, so the layout is unchanged.\n- The infinite-scroll spinner was `role=\"option\"`, an unnamed\n  unselectable option inside the listbox. Now presentational.\n- ArrowDown from the combobox targeted the first `<li>`, which for a\n  grouped list was the group heading rather than an option. It now skips\n  non-interactive rows.\n\nStill outstanding for the combobox and deliberately not attempted here:\n`aria-activedescendant`, and the search input''s `tabIndex={-1}`. Both\nrequire choosing between the APG pattern, where focus stays on the\ncombobox, and the current design, where focus moves into the options —\nthe two are mutually exclusive and the second is what the keyboard layer\nimplements today.\n\nHardcoded English in the accessibility layer becomes overridable, since\nthese strings go straight into the accessible tree and localized\napplications had no way to intervene: `loadingText` on Select and\nMultiSelectDropdown, and `openNavigationLabel` on Sidebar.\n\nAdds the accessible-name gate. jest-axe is already wired up but would\nonly have caught one of the defects in this pass and the previous one,\nbecause label and description wiring is invisible to automated scanning.\nThe gate parameterises nine components over the four id/name shapes a\ncaller can pass, which is the axis these defects actually varied along.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cristhian Fernández <14883029+CristhianF7@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"0cdabb382b3ccdbf34c7f26855b1bd3687bf5bf7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konstructio/konstruct-ui/git/trees/0cdabb382b3ccdbf34c7f26855b1bd3687bf5bf7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konstructio/konstruct-ui/git/commits/4a893753ac43853e5f421aa114589bc961d1f651","verification":{"payload":"tree 0cdabb382b3ccdbf34c7f26855b1bd3687bf5bf7\nparent a36c34751b120075a8c43efdc1bb9eb792d0e391\nauthor Cristhian Fernández <CristhianF7@gmail.com> 1787587161 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787587161 -0400\n\n🐛 fix: accessible names, error state and listbox semantics for composite controls (#702)\n\nApplies the same pass as the text-field fix to the controls built out of\nwrappers and popups, where the defects were mostly dangling id\nreferences rather than missing attributes.\n\nSelect gave its label and its combobox the same id:\n\n  <label id={m} htmlFor={m}>{label}</label>\n  <div id={m} role=\"combobox\" aria-labelledby={m} />\n\nMeasured on a labelled, required Select with an error: a duplicate id in\nthe document, `htmlFor` resolving to the label itself, `aria-labelledby`\nlanding on the label only by luck of document order, and no accessible\nname at all when `label` was omitted. Split into `-label` / `-control` /\n`-listbox` ids with an `aria-label={placeholder}` fallback.\n\nTimePicker used one identifier for four unrelated jobs — the label''s\n`htmlFor`, the control''s `aria-label`, and the hidden input''s `name` —\nwhile nothing carried it as an id. The control''s accessible name was\ntherefore the raw form name string: `<TimePicker name=\"startTime\" />`\nannounced as \"startTime\". Alongside that, `aria-expanded` was hardcoded\nto \"true\" so the trigger always reported itself as expanded,\n`aria-controls` referenced an id nothing carried, the hidden input\nsubmitted under the label id rather than `name`, and in select mode the\n`error` prop rendered nothing at all because the message lived inside the\ninput-mode branch.\n\nButtonGroup''s radiogroup had no accessible name: the label used\n`htmlFor` toward a `<div>`, which is not labelable, and the group''s\n`aria-labelledby` referenced an id nothing carried.\n\nAcross Select, PhoneNumberInput, TimePicker, ButtonGroup and ImageUpload:\nerror messages and helper text now carry ids referenced by\n`aria-describedby`, controls carry `aria-invalid`, and `isRequired` sets\n`aria-required` with the asterisk marked `aria-hidden` so it stays out of\nthe accessible name (WCAG 3.3.1). PhoneNumberInput also carried its own\ncopy of the Input `error.length >= 0` bug, treating `error=\"\"` as an\nerror state.\n\nTwo behaviour fixes surfaced by the above:\n\n- PhoneNumberInput dropped its own masking handler whenever a caller\n  passed `onChange`, because `{...delegated}` was spread after it. The\n  two are now composed.\n- DateRangePicker changes are required by the TimePicker fix and cannot\n  be split out: it renders its own label with no `htmlFor` and passed\n  `name=\"start time\"` so the buggy `aria-label` would name the field. It\n  now gets `id` and `ariaLabel` props to associate and name the control,\n  and an `ariaLabelTime` prop, because its two time fields share the\n  visible label \"Time\" and became mutually ambiguous once the form name\n  stopped disambiguating them. Visible design is unchanged.\n\nSelect listbox structure, the safe part of the combobox work:\n\n- Grouped options were rendered as a flat sibling list with the group\n  name in an `aria-hidden` `<li>`. Sighted users saw the grouping;\n  screen-reader users got an undifferentiated list. Options are now\n  wrapped in `<ul role=\"group\" aria-label={groupLabel}>`, so the tree\n  reads `listbox > group \"Europe\" > option`. Verified in a real render\n  that the nested list inherits `padding-inline-start: 0` and every row\n  keeps the same left offset and width, so the layout is unchanged.\n- The infinite-scroll spinner was `role=\"option\"`, an unnamed\n  unselectable option inside the listbox. Now presentational.\n- ArrowDown from the combobox targeted the first `<li>`, which for a\n  grouped list was the group heading rather than an option. It now skips\n  non-interactive rows.\n\nStill outstanding for the combobox and deliberately not attempted here:\n`aria-activedescendant`, and the search input''s `tabIndex={-1}`. Both\nrequire choosing between the APG pattern, where focus stays on the\ncombobox, and the current design, where focus moves into the options —\nthe two are mutually exclusive and the second is what the keyboard layer\nimplements today.\n\nHardcoded English in the accessibility layer becomes overridable, since\nthese strings go straight into the accessible tree and localized\napplications had no way to intervene: `loadingText` on Select and\nMultiSelectDropdown, and `openNavigationLabel` on Sidebar.\n\nAdds the accessible-name gate. jest-axe is already wired up but would\nonly have caught one of the defects in this pass and the previous one,\nbecause label and description wiring is invisible to automated scanning.\nThe gate parameterises nine components over the four id/name shapes a\ncaller can pass, which is the axis these defects actually varied along.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cristhian Fernández <14883029+CristhianF7@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjGpZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+cMQAACTy3E2mNW/uHlLpLsNDC2q\nGBSeYbJtHuxQ1nSrtlwl/YOK9xEDcvc45V6/mVd6HiPE4y4KZThe9fRo5WbQ9j7R\niX59Ei+R+59+FgU/UtRzGsEm+KIWvxl7LwPLingTRL4Us3VucAAB+G+jGYyNB4xo\ndVjXtJDbUuWYYXXOa8BxfTkP7zq848LVFXb8tUqMOXd9hCXppv86Ycmyy7RT1Pj1\nkoQp1L2v9W7Y9/ROOWC99K3GD6s9OoWKgJbdVP3OmvtJmHmcgLxFkTYPwtLhLa+7\nsrqpTN4WxXDEMIDfz+Bs2eLq8qUFxyUe7BwCMQQa5GSfxO81pvjFJVxSBmmUYoQi\nUeg2Qfbhx9X2E1XYHFG48LRma2gOOSWR6U3Ud7N+eCC9PYiOwpNtvcdnWPMR/n5k\nKySby6/IjXrIjQf5CxYdm0QCoqMu6MwkRTUKJNKfYXf2zfMnKqDyalAhO9EMcn5+\nBferi9lPd3vAPdH8GantbpH3ONf550kvKcS7oWvOz4kIRsbTwyFw6MzPDHD5SlTp\nkp99HPK5FcSr3V1DH3t3NVqEFn0S2fj0T9ivIhSo8auWJtpPnExsoOCcVjZ9DTXO\nYNHg4yP42P2EP/Zs7FzTBPGcqnGHI79WEWauYau918FXjmhdOjxBfj7RN71LFLtX\nqm5P86ozVviCl9vG3fX7\n=Vr6I\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-24T15:59:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/konstructio/konstruct-ui/commit/4a893753ac43853e5f421aa114589bc961d1f651","node_id":"C_kwDOM3rbOdoAKDRhODkzNzUzYWM0Mzg1M2U1ZjQyMWFhMTE0NTg5YmM5NjFkMWY2NTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/konstructio/konstruct-ui/commit/a36c34751b120075a8c43efdc1bb9eb792d0e391","sha":"a36c34751b120075a8c43efdc1bb9eb792d0e391","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konstructio/konstruct-ui/commits/a36c34751b120075a8c43efdc1bb9eb792d0e391"}],"sha":"4a893753ac43853e5f421aa114589bc961d1f651","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konstructio/konstruct-ui/commits/4a893753ac43853e5f421aa114589bc961d1f651"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14883029?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CristhianF7/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CristhianF7/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CristhianF7/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CristhianF7/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/CristhianF7","id":14883029,"login":"CristhianF7","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODgzMDI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CristhianF7/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CristhianF7/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CristhianF7/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CristhianF7/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CristhianF7/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CristhianF7","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konstructio/konstruct-ui/commits/a36c34751b120075a8c43efdc1bb9eb792d0e391/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T15:52:47Z","email":"CristhianF7@gmail.com","name":"Cristhian Fernández"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-24T15:52:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"🐛 fix: accessible names, error state and value handling for text fields (#701)\n\n* 🐛 fix: accessible names, error state and value handling for text fields\n\nCovers Checkbox, Input and TextArea. Each defect was verified against a\nreal render and, where relevant, against axe.\n\nCheckbox rendered no accessible name in three of its four call shapes.\nThe Radix root got `id={id ?? useId()}` while the label got\n`htmlFor={name ?? id}` — two different expressions that only coincided\nwhen a caller passed `id` and no `name`:\n\n  <Checkbox label=\"Accept terms\" />          for=undefined  id=:r0:\n  <Checkbox label=\"x\" name=\"n\" />            for=\"n\"        id=:r1:\n  <Checkbox label=\"x\" id=\"i\" name=\"n\" />     for=\"n\"        id=\"i\"\n\naxe reports a CRITICAL `button-name` violation for these. It survived\nbecause the label carried an onClick shim that toggled state directly, so\npointer users saw correct behaviour while the association was dead. The\nshim is removed along with the fix — with `htmlFor` correct the browser\nforwards label clicks to the Radix button natively, so keeping it would\ntoggle twice and net to zero. The existing axe assertion passed only\nbecause the fixture set `title`, which satisfies button-name; the fixture\nnow reflects real usage.\n\nInput:\n\n- `error=\"\"` was treated as an error. The guard read `error.length >= 0`,\n  true for every string. The red border, warning icon and padding all\n  applied while the message rendered nothing. Reachable through the\n  common `error={errors.name?.message ?? ''''}` idiom.\n- A caller-supplied `id` unhooked the label, because `{...delegated}` was\n  spread after `id` while `htmlFor` kept the internal `useId()`.\n- The error was never exposed to assistive tech: a bare span with no id,\n  state carried only by `data-error`. Screen-reader users got a red\n  border they cannot perceive and never heard the message (WCAG 3.3.1).\n- `isRequired` was decorative and its asterisk sat inside the accessible\n  name, announced as \"Email address star\".\n- The password reveal was gated on `!error`, so a validation failure\n  removed a focusable control from the DOM — focus was lost, and the user\n  could no longer reveal the password to fix the error being reported.\n  The gate existed because the warning icon and the button were both at\n  `right-3`. Resolved by keeping the button at `right-3` regardless of\n  state and moving the warning to `right-10` when a toggle is present,\n  with `pr-16` instead of `pr-10`. Anchoring the button means it does not\n  move under the pointer when an error appears.\n\nTextArea:\n\n- `value={initialValue ?? props.value}` made it a controlled input pinned\n  to a constant, so it could never change. Typing into a seeded textarea\n  left the DOM value untouched after a single keystroke. Now\n  `defaultValue`, guarded so a controlled `value` still wins.\n- `name` was destructured but never reached the element, so\n  `<TextArea name=\"bio\" />` never submitted.\n- A caller `id` unhooked the label, same defect as Input.\n- Props extended `InputHTMLAttributes<HTMLTextAreaElement>`, accepting\n  `type`/`checked`/`accept` and missing `cols`. Now `TextareaHTMLAttributes`.\n- Gains `error`, `helperText`, `isRequired` and the matching class-name\n  props, so validation state can be shown at all.\n\n`aria-required` is used rather than the native `required` attribute\ndeliberately: enabling real constraint validation would start blocking\nsubmits in applications running their own validation.\n\nThe password toggle''s labels become the `showPasswordLabel` /\n`hidePasswordLabel` props, so localized applications can translate them.\n\nTwo visible changes: TextArea''s label moves from a bare `<label>` to\n`Typography variant=\"labelLarge\"` to match Input, which changes its size\nand weight; and required fields no longer match an exact\n`getByLabelText(''Name'')` in downstream tests, because the label text\nstill contains the asterisk even though the accessible name no longer\ndoes — `getByRole(..., { name })` is the query that works.\n\nAdds `composeIds` to lib/utils, used here and by the composite-control\nfollow-up.\n\n* ✨ feat: align TextArea with Input styles, add error icon and isExpandable option\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cristhian Fernández <14883029+CristhianF7@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Jesús Manuel Fuentes Trejo <futjesus@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"1329a260d8d670dd98b8fcab027266f0694f0d4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konstructio/konstruct-ui/git/trees/1329a260d8d670dd98b8fcab027266f0694f0d4c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konstructio/konstruct-ui/git/commits/a36c34751b120075a8c43efdc1bb9eb792d0e391","verification":{"payload":"tree 1329a260d8d670dd98b8fcab027266f0694f0d4c\nparent 749113165faf77ac7adb0bda135e1e54c612aabc\nauthor Cristhian Fernández <CristhianF7@gmail.com> 1787586767 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787586767 -0400\n\n🐛 fix: accessible names, error state and value handling for text fields (#701)\n\n* 🐛 fix: accessible names, error state and value handling for text fields\n\nCovers Checkbox, Input and TextArea. Each defect was verified against a\nreal render and, where relevant, against axe.\n\nCheckbox rendered no accessible name in three of its four call shapes.\nThe Radix root got `id={id ?? useId()}` while the label got\n`htmlFor={name ?? id}` — two different expressions that only coincided\nwhen a caller passed `id` and no `name`:\n\n  <Checkbox label=\"Accept terms\" />          for=undefined  id=:r0:\n  <Checkbox label=\"x\" name=\"n\" />            for=\"n\"        id=:r1:\n  <Checkbox label=\"x\" id=\"i\" name=\"n\" />     for=\"n\"        id=\"i\"\n\naxe reports a CRITICAL `button-name` violation for these. It survived\nbecause the label carried an onClick shim that toggled state directly, so\npointer users saw correct behaviour while the association was dead. The\nshim is removed along with the fix — with `htmlFor` correct the browser\nforwards label clicks to the Radix button natively, so keeping it would\ntoggle twice and net to zero. The existing axe assertion passed only\nbecause the fixture set `title`, which satisfies button-name; the fixture\nnow reflects real usage.\n\nInput:\n\n- `error=\"\"` was treated as an error. The guard read `error.length >= 0`,\n  true for every string. The red border, warning icon and padding all\n  applied while the message rendered nothing. Reachable through the\n  common `error={errors.name?.message ?? ''''}` idiom.\n- A caller-supplied `id` unhooked the label, because `{...delegated}` was\n  spread after `id` while `htmlFor` kept the internal `useId()`.\n- The error was never exposed to assistive tech: a bare span with no id,\n  state carried only by `data-error`. Screen-reader users got a red\n  border they cannot perceive and never heard the message (WCAG 3.3.1).\n- `isRequired` was decorative and its asterisk sat inside the accessible\n  name, announced as \"Email address star\".\n- The password reveal was gated on `!error`, so a validation failure\n  removed a focusable control from the DOM — focus was lost, and the user\n  could no longer reveal the password to fix the error being reported.\n  The gate existed because the warning icon and the button were both at\n  `right-3`. Resolved by keeping the button at `right-3` regardless of\n  state and moving the warning to `right-10` when a toggle is present,\n  with `pr-16` instead of `pr-10`. Anchoring the button means it does not\n  move under the pointer when an error appears.\n\nTextArea:\n\n- `value={initialValue ?? props.value}` made it a controlled input pinned\n  to a constant, so it could never change. Typing into a seeded textarea\n  left the DOM value untouched after a single keystroke. Now\n  `defaultValue`, guarded so a controlled `value` still wins.\n- `name` was destructured but never reached the element, so\n  `<TextArea name=\"bio\" />` never submitted.\n- A caller `id` unhooked the label, same defect as Input.\n- Props extended `InputHTMLAttributes<HTMLTextAreaElement>`, accepting\n  `type`/`checked`/`accept` and missing `cols`. Now `TextareaHTMLAttributes`.\n- Gains `error`, `helperText`, `isRequired` and the matching class-name\n  props, so validation state can be shown at all.\n\n`aria-required` is used rather than the native `required` attribute\ndeliberately: enabling real constraint validation would start blocking\nsubmits in applications running their own validation.\n\nThe password toggle''s labels become the `showPasswordLabel` /\n`hidePasswordLabel` props, so localized applications can translate them.\n\nTwo visible changes: TextArea''s label moves from a bare `<label>` to\n`Typography variant=\"labelLarge\"` to match Input, which changes its size\nand weight; and required fields no longer match an exact\n`getByLabelText(''Name'')` in downstream tests, because the label text\nstill contains the asterisk even though the accessible name no longer\ndoes — `getByRole(..., { name })` is the query that works.\n\nAdds `composeIds` to lib/utils, used here and by the composite-control\nfollow-up.\n\n* ✨ feat: align TextArea with Input styles, add error icon and isExpandable option\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cristhian Fernández <14883029+CristhianF7@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Jesús Manuel Fuentes Trejo <futjesus@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjGjPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvl4QAFl1C1b0ntRHn21ns1Xk5F7d\n71YG7F9e4nz7xhxwl19EQJ8zpy7mmZyudGvOJ0Aniz9qfSDXzVZ1EHzwTX/HELTO\n0J83zMcabZknkMgB1ZZeAj9qulh4G0A1rnGG4PX8JXnq/y1jAdh0sbVuJWENFmG6\n9Uq7RRLzQW0/frnfjHa0FuathUZyIFskB8zfrAkceWuTuLXugA+UWBSsYKBV65dy\n9zd7JYwm4pxxLPOjjDBfDgvQuMDo7oZqyOqf2Q2NdPpBbx1e6b4Ghtff0zOXQI2e\n0imajv4dMR0DFAQBBCbLuNMpwW4R45Gg/r8wo9CgKrbksGL1LoxXKsR/qNwoF7VI\nbMqVjoOFv7gzmRMXiGStNZT5riPeRKhJsLWLaKJPQF+EUn