:"https://api.github.com/users/konstruct-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konstruct-bot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konstruct-bot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/konstructio/konstruct-ui/commit/18ef64c413b9933a269c568d85816a97d96326a4","node_id":"C_kwDOM3rbOdoAKDE4ZWY2NGM0MTNiOTkzM2EyNjljNTY4ZDg1ODE2YTk3ZDk2MzI2YTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/konstructio/konstruct-ui/commit/21b178f304a77cc93312fdbc6819e8000f2effb9","sha":"21b178f304a77cc93312fdbc6819e8000f2effb9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konstructio/konstruct-ui/commits/21b178f304a77cc93312fdbc6819e8000f2effb9"}],"sha":"18ef64c413b9933a269c568d85816a97d96326a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konstructio/konstruct-ui/commits/18ef64c413b9933a269c568d85816a97d96326a4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7634296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/futjesus","id":7634296,"login":"futjesus","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2MzQyOTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konstructio/konstruct-ui/commits/21b178f304a77cc93312fdbc6819e8000f2effb9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T16:12:03Z","email":"futjesus@gmail.com","name":"Jesús Manuel Fuentes Trejo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T16:12:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"✨ feat: add black variant to Switch and align thumb with Figma (#694)\n\nDesign updated the toggle in Figma (node 4241:23105): in light mode the\nchecked track is now black (#000000) with a white thumb instead of the\naurora green.\n\nIntroduce it as an opt-in `variant=\"black\"` rather than changing the\ndefault, so existing consumers of the green switch are untouched. In dark\nmode the black variant falls back to `aurora-500`, matching the current\ncivo dark look — a black track on a dark surface has no contrast.\n\n`switchVariants` moves from a flat class array to\n`cva(base, { variants, defaultVariants })`, following the pattern already\nused by Checkbox. The cascade is unchanged: unchecked and disabled rules\ncarry an attribute/pseudo-class selector (0,2,0) so they still beat the\nbase colour, and `dark:` / `kubefirst:` are emitted after `.bg-black`, so\nthose themes keep overriding it.\n\nFigma specs the 16px thumb at 2px from each edge of the 40x20 track,\nwhile the code used 4px. Align the base geometry for every switch:\ntranslate-x-0.5 -> translate-x-5.5.","tree":{"sha":"3d4d04c6ff96cde6cc8213a06307358f99717358","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konstructio/konstruct-ui/git/trees/3d4d04c6ff96cde6cc8213a06307358f99717358"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konstructio/konstruct-ui/git/commits/21b178f304a77cc93312fdbc6819e8000f2effb9","verification":{"payload":"tree 3d4d04c6ff96cde6cc8213a06307358f99717358\nparent 95b738b91c84cd6446f87832e3dbee799de483d5\nauthor Jesús Manuel Fuentes Trejo <futjesus@gmail.com> 1785946323 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785946323 -0400\n\n✨ feat: add black variant to Switch and align thumb with Figma (#694)\n\nDesign updated the toggle in Figma (node 4241:23105): in light mode the\nchecked track is now black (#000000) with a white thumb instead of the\naurora green.\n\nIntroduce it as an opt-in `variant=\"black\"` rather than changing the\ndefault, so existing consumers of the green switch are untouched. In dark\nmode the black variant falls back to `aurora-500`, matching the current\ncivo dark look — a black track on a dark surface has no contrast.\n\n`switchVariants` moves from a flat class array to\n`cva(base, { variants, defaultVariants })`, following the pattern already\nused by Checkbox. The cascade is unchanged: unchecked and disabled rules\ncarry an attribute/pseudo-class selector (0,2,0) so they still beat the\nbase colour, and `dark:` / `kubefirst:` are emitted after `.bg-black`, so\nthose themes keep overriding it.\n\nFigma specs the 16px thumb at 2px from each edge of the 40x20 track,\nwhile the code used 4px. Align the base geometry for every switch:\ntranslate-x-0.5 -> translate-x-5.5.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqc2DTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAe0UQADu1a820hjC1VpcKtWHfp/IQ\nwzeFLceuvXwd1Ba/78KJ53fGKoblHkD/LTixuBkhUygLu/3CXHimRG2PD4rP+Wop\nZZgR28Td3wXSdX1tvJy793cNR7+Wmoe7wtf8n1eo0eo9Q3m97kSsErBwlHKNNVyq\n9i6un2aO1eSOyMlNOeVdsecaHf3FbKHsN+CexMzWe/MzJ8Ta+C6B2DjUc8C3P+ou\nPeE4r37ZzcMjZxx2RhYpjyIreJdqQ31YNkYveohuABk/RsfLdHYih6j66wB76662\nkoq9+2hQYyZ1Ux+RFYzq9mvDcaO+RSEWIYXmMM+AT7tCKZ1blRT09NhSk7Cze17J\ndIa6S/8VCDV0Ww/QnPyOh3dIUPFIy4X1wFP0r6CWWRCY8ofA30yJTbj0EGQJ94DX\njH3+aBopQOrvwxAIJP99zMzBabei66yZQbWFabGVuMDzYEyWeim1kN3Rg++bZkED\nNEHHgmmcjbSRbNhX1OZ9hQZedV0Tp+JbuPul6RKPYifq+c8q07QP30usQmwzKfx/\nvBNS9pTzyoUy2UA1rRrgmDCNTzoDeJX0yP7pQYe8Uj+wXbAGzQH6ULLmu8943nII\nW/8SrwsVxgfRZh8vTVw4xK65I7S8OsJsehCq3JwYchvGMiaDz8F426RXF+jwp1wA\ntxngyRaM74x0XlS7fv6r\n=QEgX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-05T16:12:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/konstructio/konstruct-ui/commit/21b178f304a77cc93312fdbc6819e8000f2effb9","node_id":"C_kwDOM3rbOdoAKDIxYjE3OGYzMDRhNzdjYzkzMzEyZmRiYzY4MTllODAwMGYyZWZmYjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/konstructio/konstruct-ui/commit/95b738b91c84cd6446f87832e3dbee799de483d5","sha":"95b738b91c84cd6446f87832e3dbee799de483d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konstructio/konstruct-ui/commits/95b738b91c84cd6446f87832e3dbee799de483d5"}],"sha":"21b178f304a77cc93312fdbc6819e8000f2effb9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konstructio/konstruct-ui/commits/21b178f304a77cc93312fdbc6819e8000f2effb9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7634296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/futjesus","id":7634296,"login":"futjesus","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2MzQyOTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konstructio/konstruct-ui/commits/95b738b91c84cd6446f87832e3dbee799de483d5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T15:46:08Z","email":"futjesus@gmail.com","name":"Jesús Manuel Fuentes Trejo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T15:46:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"🐛 fix: select all re-selects items after deselection in Filter multiselects (#693)\n\nChecking Select All after unchecking items left the item checkboxes\nvisually unchecked while the internal state considered them selected,\nso Apply emitted options the user could not see as checked.\n\nThe item checked-state predicate ignored the isRemoved tombstone flag\nwhile isAllSelected respected it, so the key-remount hack never fired\non re-select. Fix the root cause by making Checkbox support a real\ncontrolled checked prop (uncontrolled behavior unchanged when omitted)\nand dropping the key/defaultChecked remount hack in BadgeMultiSelect\nand TextMultiSelect.\n\nAlso in the shared hook: unchecking Select All now tombstones every\noption (previously a no-op), checking it preserves isApplied flags so\nthe trigger badge count no longer resets mid-edit, re-checking a\ntombstoned option clears the flag instead of appending a duplicate,\nreopening resets stale tombstones on applied entries, and all state\nupdates are functional. Checkboxes now expose accessible names via\naria-label, enabling role-based queries in the new regression tests.","tree":{"sha":"5d8a2b1b4bc46356c81901533e054adea47d0e76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konstructio/konstruct-ui/git/trees/5d8a2b1b4bc46356c81901533e054adea47d0e76"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konstructio/konstruct-ui/git/commits/95b738b91c84cd6446f87832e3dbee799de483d5","verification":{"payload":"tree 5d8a2b1b4bc46356c81901533e054adea47d0e76\nparent 8ffd68ba643784e6509bc048313317c319ed8481\nauthor Jesús Manuel Fuentes Trejo <futjesus@gmail.com> 1785944768 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785944768 -0400\n\n🐛 fix: select all re-selects items after deselection in Filter multiselects (#693)\n\nChecking Select All after unchecking items left the item checkboxes\nvisually unchecked while the internal state considered them selected,\nso Apply emitted options the user could not see as checked.\n\nThe item checked-state predicate ignored the isRemoved tombstone flag\nwhile isAllSelected respected it, so the key-remount hack never fired\non re-select. Fix the root cause by making Checkbox support a real\ncontrolled checked prop (uncontrolled behavior unchanged when omitted)\nand dropping the key/defaultChecked remount hack in BadgeMultiSelect\nand TextMultiSelect.\n\nAlso in the shared hook: unchecking Select All now tombstones every\noption (previously a no-op), checking it preserves isApplied flags so\nthe trigger badge count no longer resets mid-edit, re-checking a\ntombstoned option clears the flag instead of appending a duplicate,\nreopening resets stale tombstones on applied entries, and all state\nupdates are functional. Checkboxes now expose accessible names via\naria-label, enabling role-based queries in the new regression tests.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqc1rACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2SYQAB8HKlXmJC79xIoeyQMQpo8Z\ngp1NaaQO1/2UpLkhwThFtBW89t9aPZRsYT65MIhbxOVGTTNjG1j2E5aKJXmXXjGN\n7xo5xoN/YZ7bfDEEpKBacfe0Oblb+aG54aDddKUrBIm6BwxxULsJHhaK8AKYZHE9\neihmHQfIDfj5+QiNJvEXme5aNSn7IICLe1hiyrI00wk21Xy4tqsqqqAEVkzzgXM5\n2tJPyq3/6Y+5zPYAeK3zekBd0FMwcIuP6hbnCePDwEleP66HoJVgdyzdhU89VlEy\n3zsRrHi9fpB9OgkA1LCR42fWrEyvO+5i34S/PZRh+O6xh+WWiwZh8WztSYiBdOjX\nu8x2KEaxHO0G0xvxf2nt/l+rs9spxB8g3OI9IqHhySD4tat