","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konstruct-bot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/konstructio/konstruct-ui/commit/a0bf10d155d4a4035dbbf6d2157c1908b22d1b53","node_id":"C_kwDOM3rbOdoAKGEwYmYxMGQxNTVkNGE0MDM1ZGJiZjZkMjE1N2MxOTA4YjIyZDFiNTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/konstructio/konstruct-ui/commit/78abade27904560b425390e2ba519d0f445a4979","sha":"78abade27904560b425390e2ba519d0f445a4979","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konstructio/konstruct-ui/commits/78abade27904560b425390e2ba519d0f445a4979"}],"sha":"a0bf10d155d4a4035dbbf6d2157c1908b22d1b53","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konstructio/konstruct-ui/commits/a0bf10d155d4a4035dbbf6d2157c1908b22d1b53"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7634296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/futjesus","id":7634296,"login":"futjesus","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2MzQyOTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konstructio/konstruct-ui/commits/78abade27904560b425390e2ba519d0f445a4979/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T16:50:24Z","email":"futjesus@gmail.com","name":"Jesús Manuel Fuentes Trejo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T16:50:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"🐛 fix: let consumers retheme Sidebar options through className (#685)\n\n* 🐛 fix: let consumers retheme Sidebar options through className\n\nThe NavigationOption hover/active colors lived in Sidebar.css keyed on\n`li[role=''option'']`. #677 dropped that invalid role from the `<li>`, so the\nrules stopped matching and every consumer theming through the\n`--konstruct-sidebar-hover-bg` / `--konstruct-sidebar-active-bg` custom\nproperties silently fell back to the library default.\n\nRather than re-point the selector, move the styling into the cva variants:\na descriptor selector like `.konstruct-sidebar li:hover` (0,2,2) outranks a\nsingle utility class (0,1,0), so a consumer could never win through\n`className` even when the selector did match.\n\n- Drop the dead `li[role=''option'']` rules from Sidebar.css; the variants\n  already cover the layout, padding and anchor styling they mirrored\n- Add the one rule that was not mirrored (`shrink-0`) to the variants\n- Prefix the active classes with `data-[active=true]:` so tailwind-merge\n  detects the conflict against a consumer override and drops the default\n- Remove the now-unused `text-black` and duplicated `font-normal`\n- Cover both directions with tests: an override wins, no override keeps the\n  default\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: `--konstruct-sidebar-hover-bg`, `--konstruct-sidebar-hover-color`,\n`--konstruct-sidebar-active-bg` and `--konstruct-sidebar-active-color` no longer\ndo anything. Pass the colors to `NavigationOption` via `className` instead:\n`hover:bg-metal-800 data-[active=true]:bg-metal-800`.\n\n* 📝 docs: tighten the no-comments rule to cover change rationale and CSS","tree":{"sha":"1f0ec49c80a4a2e68d9c14966be456b54e8aae76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konstructio/konstruct-ui/git/trees/1f0ec49c80a4a2e68d9c14966be456b54e8aae76"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konstructio/konstruct-ui/git/commits/78abade27904560b425390e2ba519d0f445a4979","verification":{"payload":"tree 1f0ec49c80a4a2e68d9c14966be456b54e8aae76\nparent 3d4e0b5e1ab35c4a182faaed01fd04a16a374f29\nauthor Jesús Manuel Fuentes Trejo <futjesus@gmail.com> 1785171024 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785171024 -0400\n\n🐛 fix: let consumers retheme Sidebar options through className (#685)\n\n* 🐛 fix: let consumers retheme Sidebar options through className\n\nThe NavigationOption hover/active colors lived in Sidebar.css keyed on\n`li[role=''option'']`. #677 dropped that invalid role from the `<li>`, so the\nrules stopped matching and every consumer theming through the\n`--konstruct-sidebar-hover-bg` / `--konstruct-sidebar-active-bg` custom\nproperties silently fell back to the library default.\n\nRather than re-point the selector, move the styling into the cva variants:\na descriptor selector like `.konstruct-sidebar li:hover` (0,2,2) outranks a\nsingle utility class (0,1,0), so a consumer could never win through\n`className` even when the selector did match.\n\n- Drop the dead `li[role=''option'']` rules from Sidebar.css; the variants\n  already cover the layout, padding and anchor styling they mirrored\n- Add the one rule that was not mirrored (`shrink-0`) to the variants\n- Prefix the active classes with `data-[active=true]:` so tailwind-merge\n  detects the conflict against a consumer override and drops the default\n- Remove the now-unused `text-black` and duplicated `font-normal`\n- Cover both directions with tests: an override wins, no override keeps the\n  default\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: `--konstruct-sidebar-hover-bg`, `--konstruct-sidebar-hover-color`,\n`--konstruct-sidebar-active-bg` and `--konstruct-sidebar-active-color` no longer\ndo anything. Pass the colors to `NavigationOption` via `className` instead:\n`hover:bg-metal-800 data-[active=true]:bg-metal-800`.\n\n* 📝 docs: tighten the no-comments rule to cover change rationale and CSS","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZ4xQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAf58QAGUPBl/XyZlFOdTsxW9JAlh2\n4Sl/HuDXRyhJH