://github.com/konstructio/konstruct-ui/commit/c574c283653991c0d7509daee166e89421b47450","sha":"c574c283653991c0d7509daee166e89421b47450","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konstructio/konstruct-ui/commits/c574c283653991c0d7509daee166e89421b47450"}],"sha":"a1b1a5b13e8998ce98e28ac1fd2a31cd59bd21c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konstructio/konstruct-ui/commits/a1b1a5b13e8998ce98e28ac1fd2a31cd59bd21c8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7634296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/futjesus","id":7634296,"login":"futjesus","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2MzQyOTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/futjesus","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konstructio/konstruct-ui/commits/c574c283653991c0d7509daee166e89421b47450/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-21T20:56:51Z","email":"futjesus@gmail.com","name":"Jesús Manuel Fuentes Trejo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-21T20:56:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"🐛 fix: VirtualizedTable query lifecycle + errorState/headerContent/scroll container (#666)\n\n* 🐛 fix: rework VirtualizedTable query lifecycle so the skeleton never strands\n\nThe provider seeded initialData on every query key, forcing isLoading to\nstay false and the skeleton to gate on isFetching. Consumers suppressed\nthe resulting poll flicker with notifyOnChangeProps: [''data'',''error''],\nwhich silently dropped the isFetching:false re-render whenever a refetch\nresolved to structurally-equal data, stranding the table on the skeleton.\n\n- Seed initialData only for the first cache entry and only when rows were\n  provided, so isLoading regains meaning (skeleton on initial load and\n  key changes, silent background refetches)\n- Merge consumer notifyOnChangeProps with the props the provider reads so\n  internal re-renders can never be suppressed\n- Move queryFn side effects into an effect keyed on dataUpdatedAt, which\n  changes on every successful fetch regardless of structural sharing\n- Gate Skeleton/Pagination/WrapperBody on tableLoading instead of\n  tableFetching, expose tableError and headerContent through the context\n- Stop mutating the consumer id array when building the query key\n- Move root tests into tests/ and add fetch integration coverage\n\n* ✨ feat: add errorState, headerContent and scroll container to VirtualizedTable\n\n- errorState?: ReactNode | ((error: Error) => ReactNode) renders in place\n  of rows when the query failed and there is nothing to show; background\n  refetch failures keep the current rows. With React Query''s default\n  retry it appears after retries; queryOptions={{ retry: false }} shows\n  it immediately\n- headerContent renders a full-width band inside the thead above the\n  column headers (scrolls with the table, visible in every state) and\n  takes over the top rounded corners, including the expand-column handoff\n- classNameScrollContainer opts into a horizontal scroll region wrapping\n  the table body and pagination bar while the filter row stays fixed to\n  the container width\n- Stable kvt-* class hooks on every section (filter, search, header,\n  band, body, rows, cells, states, pagination) so consumers can restyle\n  any part from outside\n- Stories for HeaderContent, ErrorState and HorizontalScrollWithFilters\n\n* ✨ feat: portal Filter dropdowns and rework the page-size dropdown\n\nFilter dropdown menus were hand-rolled absolute divs that any overflow\ncontainer clipped (overflow-x forces overflow-y), blocking the new table\nscroll region. All five dropdowns now share a Radix Popover based\nFilterDropdown (portaled, collision-aware, Escape to close); the manual\nmousedown outside-click handlers are gone because they would close the\nportaled menus from inside.\n\nThe pagination page-size dropdown is rebuilt on Radix Popover reusing\nthe Select variants: direction ''auto'' flips up only when the viewport\nhas no room below (dropdownPaginationDirection fixes it to ''up''/''down''),\nand it portals automatically when classNameScrollContainer is set. The\n150px spacer that reserved room below the bar is no longer needed.\n\n* ♻️ refactor: drop valueless useCallback/useMemo in VirtualizedTable\n\nRemoves memoization whose result feeds inline arrows or plain DOM\nelements, plus trivial boolean/number computations. Callbacks exposed\nthrough the table context, column-identity memos and the search debounce\nstay memoized because consumers depend on their identity.\n\n* 🔧 chore: pin vite-plugin-dts entryRoot so dist keeps the lib/ layout\n\n* 📝 docs: add code-comments rule to CLAUDE.md\n\n* 🔧 chore: sync package-lock so npm ci resolves the full tree\n\n* 🎨 style: use canonical negative translate classes in Input\n\n* 🔧 chore: regenerate package-lock from main with a clean full resolution\n\nnpm 11 prunes transitive deps of wasm platform packages when resolving\nnext to an existing node_modules, which left the lock missing @emnapi\nentries npm ci requires. Regenerated from origin/main''s lock in a clean\ndirectory; validated with npm ci --dry-run on npm 10 and 11.","tree":{"sha":"7abf013f89e937cda9bc5a6b64a1ce5c53c80f75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konstructio/konstruct-ui/git/trees/7abf013f89e937cda9bc5a6b64a1ce5c53c80f75"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konstructio/konstruct-ui/git/commits/c574c283653991c0d7509daee166e89421b47450","verification":{"payload":"tree 7abf013f89e937cda9bc5a6b64a1ce5c53c80f75\nparent 44e76d3927e6d67570e985ff149a2f9f966c0cc4\nauthor Jesús Manuel Fuentes Trejo <futjesus@gmail.com> 1784667411 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784667411 -0400\n\n🐛 fix: VirtualizedTable query lifecycle + errorState/headerContent/scroll container (#666)\n\n* 🐛 fix: rework VirtualizedTable query lifecycle so the skeleton never strands\n\nThe provider seeded initialData on every query key, forcing isLoading to\nstay false and the skeleton to gate on isFetching. Consumers suppressed\nthe resulting poll flicker with notifyOnChangeProps: [''data'',''error''],\nwhich silently dropped the isFetching:false re-render whenever a refetch\nresolved to structurally-equal data, stranding the table on the skeleton.\n\n- Seed initialData only for the first cache entry and only when rows were\n  provided, so isLoading regains meaning (skeleton on initial load and\n  key changes, silent background refetches)\n- Merge consumer notifyOnChangeProps with the props the provider reads so\n  internal re-renders can never be suppressed\n- Move queryFn side effects into an effect keyed on dataUpdatedAt, which\n  changes on every successful fetch regardless of structural sharing\n- Gate Skeleton/Pagination/WrapperBody on tableLoading instead of\n  tableFetching, expose tableError and headerContent through the context\n- Stop mutating the consumer id array when building the query key\n- Move root tests into tests/ and add fetch integration coverage\n\n* ✨ feat: add errorState, headerContent and scroll container to VirtualizedTable\n\n- errorState?: ReactNode | ((error: Error) => ReactNode) renders in place\n  of rows when the query failed and there is nothing to show; background\n  refetch failures keep the current rows. With React Query''s default\n  retry it appears after retries; queryOptions={{ retry: false }} shows\n  it immediately\n- headerContent renders a full-width band inside the thead above the\n  column headers (scrolls with the table, visible in every state) and\n  takes over the top rounded corners, including the expand-column handoff\n- classNameScrollContainer opts into a horizontal scroll region wrapping\n  the table body and pagination bar while the filter row stays fixed to\n  the container width\n- Stable kvt-* class hooks on every section (filter, search, header,\n  band, body, rows, cells, states, pagination) so consumers can restyle\n  any part from outside\n- Stories for HeaderContent, ErrorState and HorizontalScrollWithFilters\n\n* ✨ feat: portal Filter dropdowns and rework the page-size dropdown\n\nFilter dropdown menus were hand-rolled absolute divs that any overflow\ncontainer clipped (overflow-x forces overflow-y), blocking the new table\nscroll region. All five dropdowns now share a Radix Popover based\nFilterDropdown (portaled, collision-aware, Escape to close); the manual\nmousedown outside-click handlers are gone because they would close the\nportaled menus from inside.\n\nThe pagination page-size dropdown is rebuilt on Radix Popover reusing\nthe Select variants: direction ''auto'' flips up only when the viewport\nhas no room below (dropdownPaginationDirection fixes it to ''up''/''down''),\nand it portals automatically when classNameScrollContainer is set. The\n150px spacer that reserved room below the bar is no longer needed.\n\n* ♻️ refactor: drop valueless useCallback/useMemo in VirtualizedTable\n\nRemoves memoization whose result feeds inline arrows or plain DOM\nelements, plus trivial boolean/number computations. Callbacks exposed\nthrough the table context, column-identity memos and the search debounce\nstay memoized because consumers depend on their identity.\n\n* 🔧 chore: pin vite-plugin-dts entryRoot so dist keeps the lib/ layout\n\n* 📝 docs: add code-comments rule to CLAUDE.md\n\n* 🔧 chore: sync package-lock so npm ci resolves the full tree\n\n* 🎨 style: use canonical negative translate classes in Input\n\n* 🔧 chore: regenerate package-lock from main with a clean full resolution\n\nnpm 11 prunes transitive deps of wasm platform packages when resolving\nnext to an existing node_modules, which left the lock missing @emnapi\nentries npm ci requires. Regenerated from origin/main''s lock in a clean\ndirectory; validated with npm ci --dry-run on npm 10 and 11.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqX90TCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2pwQAFZoCLP04xN7Z7Uxg6HG694l\nMD49ryH79Cbhp+7IqnZ0yA9dKu8c2+d32aTQ7R/uJp7lTJ0Ped8X7VaJoIV3IX2h\nVIRmHcHlZjN20sJU4Cw91ZQueAVBlUXvV3H5wl+AI/0GTIhizY+YIB2oqYtQup/X\nClPwDt9aXNL8bZiNYsq6kJ4PuG6QeMUiwSRiOO+5K9scxQnaoQLEIzPVsl0vZQJW\n79FoRBSXTW0HuD8crtO8d2hiJGnPj0iCnFrgjLgQGV3bJ6SgvZMbcNbZk7ppjFtB\nNyLq/oIES8bVxLOCu6BVRogRhLt9cIJhoFqx83DYE+KwOB6wziRW9SRG7waY/ave\nlcPWvwdJB438By5ACZKFzC9Q+CnsoGSyygX1elq56j1t3V5GN8ho3Q+nthhFadDc\n5IAMe9iMsy8b3I5UZmMEfKtD1M/L/3XnSxJIYxmtIzssORaaINkYvaIGPwAKdCRF\n2ANxlwrOStBSr6dhP2MyNj/34N89YNDY4QWCt3lfTv1NxXh94xi24acsJjeEgN8v\nuiWG3pq6SjS0W20B6sCEBZuPh5cA/a9H1EWjsoIbS4mXdmVos+YRwnkPDPgjUtAI\npYfmsx+Y7HCuLmf7Ew1ITZvHswIBYQbZHY29wzVGm3fbmn+c6NzVcP7g4TMY3u6p\nJfn+pHUYBIChgKFCnhG0\n=ALfX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-21T20:56:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/u